\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1043}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|std::regex::node~} holds regexes as nodes of a table. Every constructor applies the rewrite rules and then looks the result up among the existing nodes, so equal regexes are the same number. \code{\verb~|derive~} gives the derivative of a node by a class of bytes, \code{\verb~|add~} the node of a \code{\verb~|ByteRegex~}, and \code{\verb~|refine~} the classes of its sets. See [normalization](design-regex-derivatives-normalization). \pr{1043}.}
